WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.875
The paper contributes CABINET, short for Content
Relevance-Based Noise Reduction.

00:00:03.955 --> 00:00:07.830
It has two cooperating parts.

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:11.785
First,

00:00:11.865 --> 00:00:15.740
an Unsupervised Relevance Scorer assigns a soft
relevance weight to every table token

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:19.695
and is trained differentiably alongside the
question-answering model.

00:00:19.775 --> 00:00:23.650
Second,

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.605
a weakly-supervised module generates a parsing
statement describing which rows and columns matter,

00:00:27.685 --> 00:00:31.560
then highlights the corresponding cells to produce
a cell-based relevance signal.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.515
Together they let the model focus without
discarding content,

00:00:35.595 --> 00:00:39.470
and they deliver new state of the art on three
benchmarks along with stronger robustness to noise and to large tables.
